<title>PERU: Peru's June mined tin output rises 3.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's June mined tin output rises 3.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's tin output rose 3.1 percent to 2,584 tonnes in June from the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from Energy and Mines Ministry released Thursday.</p>
<p>Tin output rose 12 percent to 13,839 tonnes in the first half of the year from the same period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Minsur, Peru's only tin miner, is the world's third largest tin producer. The company operates the San Rafael mine in the southern highlands.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
